    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/HHT_IAP26/performances/HHT23IS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/HHT_IAP26/performances/HHT23IS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Inside American Pie"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p><i>So bye, bye Miss American Pie<br>\n\nDrove my Chevy to the levee but the levee was dry<br>\n\nAnd them good ol' boys were drinkin' whiskey and rye<br>\n\nSingin', 'This'll be the day that I die.<br>\n\nThis'll be the day that I die.'</i><br><br>\n\nSure, you know the chorus, but do you know the stories behind the song?<br><br>\n\nA lot of people know that 'American Pie' was written by Don McLean to commemorate the plane crash that killed Buddy Holly, Richie Valens and The Big Bopper. What's less known is that the song is jam packed with references to other fascinating events in history.<br><br>\n\nJoin Mike Ross and a group of homegrown mega-talent, Alicia Toner, Brielle Ansems, Greg Gale, and Kirk White, as they dive deep into the mysteries of this #1 hit - What happened that tragic night in 1959? How do The Beatles, Bob Dylan, Janis Joplin, and Charles Manson all fit in? Why were the Rolling Stones blamed for a murder? And who was Miss American Pie?<br><br>\n\nThis summer at Harmony House, we're bringing you a concert you won't want to miss: a night of investigation, revelation, and roof-shaking music.</p>\n<p><b>If you would like to make a reservation to enjoy dinner before the show, please call the venue at: 902-964-2255 or email them at <a href='mailto:harmonyhousePEIresos@gmail.com'>harmonyhousePEIresos@gmail.com</a>!<br>Please note: On 2pm matinee days, The Lounge is open for dinner reservations 3:30pm onward, after the 2pm performance.<br><br>\nFor ticket details, visit Harmony House Theatre on-line at <a href='https://harmonyhousepei.com/' target='_blank'><u>harmonyhousepei.com</u></a> or call the box office at 1-888-311-9090.</i></b></p>\n\n<p><b>Harmony House Gift Certificates are not redeemable through Ticketpro. Please contact Harmony House directly to redeem.</b></p>\n\n<p><b><font size='+1'>TICKET PURCHASES ARE FINAL AND NON-REFUNDABLE</b></font></p>\n\n\n<style>\n.location-page-temp {\n    display: block!important;\n}\n</style>\n\n"
      }
    ],
