    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1699818368/performances/MCC24IS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1699818368/performances/MCC24IS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Les Barocudas - Debut Atlantic Classical Series"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p>From their very first album, La peste (ATMA Classique, 2020), Les Barocudas distinguished themselves through their originality. Inspired by the plague epidemics of the 17th century, this recording for three musicians (violin, viola da gamba/bass violin, and keyboards) offers a program rich in contrasts and atmospheres, acclaimed by both critics and audiences. Nominated for the JUNO and Opus Awards, the album was recognized by CBC Music as one of the best classical productions of the year.</p><br>\n\n<p>Since then, the ensemble has expanded—incorporating recorder, organ, harpsichord, and baroque harp—and has continued its artistic trajectory with a new acclaimed album, Basta Parlare! (2023), also nominated for a JUNO Award. This recording confirms the group's originality, its passion for the repertoires of the 17th and 18th centuries, and its ability to make this music resonate with intelligence and passion.</p><br>\n\n<p>The performances of Les Barocudas—both in concert and on recordings—are characterized by a keen sense of musical expression, natural stage presence, and strong ensemble cohesion.</p><br>\n\n<p>Far from static reconstructions, their performances offer a vibrant, contemporary, and generous interpretation of early music, breathing new life into forgotten Baroque treasures.</p><br>\n\n<style>\n@media screen and (max-width: 600px){iframe{width:100%;}}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
