      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "John Wing - Go East, Old Man - With Special Guest Dan Mitchelmore"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<b>⭐ The Man, The Myth, The Credits ⭐</b><br><br>\n\nJohn Wing's resume reads like a history book of late-night television and world-renowned comedy stages. He has amassed over 350 television appearances across North America. Take a look at some of his incredible career highlights:<br><br>\n\n<b>Late-Night Royalty:</b> One of the rare Canadian comics to perform on The Tonight Show six times, spanning eras with both Johnny Carson and Jay Leno.<br>\n\n<b>Prime-Time Success:</b> Captivated millions as a standout semi-finalist on NBC's America's Got Talent (Season 8).<br>\n\n<b>Festival Favorite: </b>A certified heavy hitter on the festival circuit, including 10 appearances at the prestigious Montreal Just For Laughs Festival, plus regulars at the Winnipeg, Toronto, and Halifax Comedy Festivals.<br>\n\n<b>Radio Icon:</b> A beloved voice nationwide as a frequent guest on CBC Radio's The Debaters, and the creator/host of his own CBC Radio series, Man, Woman & Child.<br>\n\n<b>Author & Poet: </b>Proving his wit translates beautifully to the page, John has published multiple books of poetry and a hilarious memoir about his early days in stand-up, Ventriloquism for Dummies.<br><br>\n\nJohn will be joined by Halifax comedian Dan Mitchelmore, one of the rising young voices in Nova Scotia's comedy scene. Dan has been performing stand-up across the city and province for the past two years. He's known for his approachable style, crowd engagement, and ability to create a fun atmosphere wherever he perform<br><br>\n\nJohn will also be using a special Guitar during the show which will be donated to Guitars for Vets after the tour. We welcome Vets and Family members to sign the guitar case or place a card in it with a special message for the Vet that will receive it.\n\n\n\n<style>\n\n@media screen and (max-width:728px) {\niframe{width:100%!important;}\n}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
