    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<!--<p>The 15<sup>th</sup> edition of Devour! The Food Film Fest, taking place from October 20 to 26, 2025. <b>Devour! Montréal All-Stars</b> will bring the city's most exciting culinary creators, featuring soon-to-be Michelin-star chefs, and Oscar-winning and Canadian filmmakers, to Wolfville.</p>\n\n<p><b>Devour! Box Office & Retail Shop</b> - Located in the Devour! Studios at 360 Main Street, Wolfville<br>\nOctober 20-21, 2025 - 9:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m.<br>\nOctober 22-24, 2025 - 9:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m.<br>\nOctober 25, 2025 - 9:00 a.m. to 10:00 p.m.<br>\nOctober 26, 2025 - 10:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m.</p>\n\n<p><b>Devour! Satellite Box Offices</b> - The box office opens half an hour before film and event programming in the lobby of the Al Whittle Theatre at 450 Main Street and at selected event locations</p>\t-->\t\n\n<style>\n.filter-page-show-temp {display: block !important}\n.location-page-temp {display: none!important;}\n</style>"
      },
      {
        "@value": "<p>For the past decade, Devour! and Nourish Nova Scotia have proudly presented a captivating series of films designed for youth, focusing on important topics such as sugar, farming, food waste, and climate change. This initiative has reached over 4,500 school children across Nova Scotia, providing enriching screenings and workshops.</p>\n\n<p>This two-hour experience blends films with interactive post-screening discussions facilitated by the Nourish Nova Scotia team and hands-on cooking classes led by chefs Peter Dewar and Paul Thimot, along with students from the Nova Scotia Community College's culinary program. By teaching cooking skills to young people, we aim to highlight the significance of food in family life, enhance societal and physical health, and deepen their understanding of local food sourcing and its vital role in our regional economy. Join us for this wonderful opportunity to learn and grow through the lens of food and film!</p>\n\n<p>Films will be followed by a facilitated post-screening chat with Nourish Nova Scotia and a hands-on culinary workshop led by Chefs and students from the Nova Scotia Community College's culinary program. This year's recipe is a Rice Bowl with local seaweed, vegetables, and a honey garlic dressing.</p>\n\n<p><b>Teachers, please email our Box Office at <a href='mailto:tickets@devourfest.com'>tickets@devourfest.com</a> to book. Nothing is sold out yet, there are holds for schools on a first come, first served basis.<br>\nTicket Price for the Film & Workshop Bundle: $5.00 per student</b></p>\n\n<style>\n.filter-page-show-temp {display: block !important}\n.location-page-temp {display: none!important;}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
