      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "APC Big Band & Backhouse Brass - Antigonish Jazz Fest"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "\n\n\n<p><b>APC Big Band - 2:00 p.m.</b>: The APC Big Band has been together in various configurations for more than 25 years. Initially a Dixieland combo based in Antigonish, the band transitioned to a small jazz orchestra before expanding to a standard big band format, with complete trumpet, trombone, saxophone, and rhythm sections, male and female vocalists. At present, APC consists of 24 musicians from Antigonish, Pictou, and Colchester Counties. Our repertoire includes big band / swing standards, Latin and contemporary jazz pieces, and pop selections. We are looking forward to our second Antigonish Jazz Fest performance on Thursday, November 5, and hope to see you there!</p>\n\n\n\n\n<p><b>Backhouse Brass - 3:10 p.m.</b>: Backhouse Brass is a six-piece brass ensemble from Cape Breton, Nova Scotia, known for their creative, high-energy arrangements of popular music. Originally formed as a high school project, the group found its footing during the 2020 pandemic, dedicating their time to arranging, rehearsing, and entertaining crowds along the Sydney boardwalk.</p>\n\n<p>Six years later, Backhouse Brass has become a fixture of Nova Scotia's live music scene, earning a reputation for electrifying performances that engage audiences of all ages. In the summer of 2025, the group released their debut original composition, 'Liquorice Sandwich,' on all major streaming platforms, with additional original music set to follow.</p>\n\n\n<style>\n.location-page-temp {\n    display: block!important;\n}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
