      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "CHANDRA - Antigonish Jazz Fest"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "\n\n\n<p>CHANDRA is a collaborative project that reimagines the traditional music of the Iberian Peninsula from a jazz perspective. The quintet creates original compositions and arrangements, exploring what folklore means to each of its members within their respective cultural and artistic contexts. Improvisation plays a fundamental role, both as a musical practice and as a way to keep tradition alive and evolving.</p>\n\n<p>The group brings together five artists with diverse backgrounds and a shared commitment to creative exploration: María Fajardo and Nené Álvarez on vocals, Javier Galiana on piano, Javier Delgado on double bass, and Guillermo Martín-Viana on drums and percussion. María Fajardo is a jazz vocalist and educator based in Madrid, active in the contemporary jazz scenes of Asia and Latin America. Nené Álvarez, a performing artist in theater and dance, brings a multidisciplinary sensibility shaped by her musical beginnings within her family and her growing commitment to music. Pianist and composer Javier Galiana is a key figure in Andalusian jazz, fusing flamenco, theater, and orchestral composition in his work. Bassist Javier Delgado bridges classical traditions and jazz, with a career encompassing collaborations in Europe, North Africa, and Asia. Guillermo Martín Viana, percussionist and multimedia artist, moves between jazz, experimental music, and interdisciplinary performance, connecting sound, images, and live interaction.</p>\n\n<p>Together, they create a space where traditional forms, the language of jazz, and improvisation converge, offering a contemporary approach to folk music that is both personal and collective.</p>\n\n\n<style>\n.location-page-temp {\n    display: block!important;\n}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
