  {
    "@id": "https://ticketpro.ca/event/1701914524",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2026-12-08T19:30:00-04:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "https://ticketpro.ca/place/12445250"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/api/v1/resources/1701966301.jpeg?version=1"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/offers": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/genid/cfb48c1d38b051bf"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1701364997/performances/MCC08LS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1701364997/performances/MCC08LS26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Home For Christmas"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<p>Step in from the cold and into a glow of candlelight, story, and song. Home For Christmas gathers three cherished East Coast voices—Heather Rankin, Rachel MacLean, and Dale Miller—for a heartfelt evening where Celtic roots mingle with seasonal classics, and every chorus feels like a hug.</p><br>\n \n<p>Heather Rankin brings the unmistakable warmth and lilt that made The Rankin Family beloved across Canada. Drawing on her Cape Breton heritage, she blends traditional influences with tender, modern touches—shaping carols and winter hymns into intimate moments that feel both timeless and new. Her holiday recordings, including Imagine, showcase the expressive vocals and gentle storytelling that turn familiar melodies into memories-in-the-making.</p><br>\n\n<p>From the Annapolis Valley, Rachel MacLean adds a shimmer of serenity and joy. A lifelong performer who first charmed audiences with her sister in the duo The MacLeans, Rachel's solo work—spanning inspirational, folk, and seasonal music—glows with sincerity. Songs from Beyond the Rain and her Christmas album, Falling Snow, carry the hush of a first snowfall and the quiet hope of candlelit midnight—pure, beautiful, and uplifting.</p><br>\n\n<p>Dora Award-winner Dale Miller rounds out the trio with theatrical flair and heart. With more than three decades on stages across Canada and beyond, Dale's polished presence and rich vocals bring sparkle to big-band crooners, reverence to sacred standards, and a playful wink to festive favorites. From concert halls to stadium anthems, his voice fills the room with warmth, good cheer, and just the right dash of showmanship.</p><br>\n\n<p>Together, these three artists weave harmonies like garlands—Celtic-folk textures entwined with piano, guitar, and classic arrangements—inviting you to sing along, laugh, and linger in the glow of the season. Expect cherished carols, winter lullabies, and stories of home, family, and the small, shining moments that make Christmastime magical.</p><br>\n\n<p>Home For Christmas is more than a concert—it's a gathering. Pull up a chair, warm your hands around the music, and let Heather, Rachel, and Dale lead you gently toward the heart of the holidays.</p><br>\n\n<style>\n@media screen and (max-width: 600px){iframe{width:100%;}}\n</style>"
      }
    ],
