    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://tproatlantic.ticketpro.ca/en/pages/1650109597"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "The Nova Scotia Seafood Academy: Tide to Table: A Nova Scotia Seafood Masterclass - May 12-14, 2027"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "<br>Experience the rich maritime heritage of Nova Scotia like never before! The Nova Scotia Seafood Academy is calling all food enthusiasts, travelers, and industry professionals to embark on a culinary adventure that celebrates our province's incredible seafood bounty. Join us in sharpening your culinary skills with our exclusive new program, the only one of its kind in Atlantic Canada!<br><br>\n\nAt the Nova Scotia Seafood Academy, we believe that cooking is not just a skill but a journey through culture and community. Our unique curriculum is designed to deepen your understanding of seafood preparation while highlighting the importance of sustainable practices and local sourcing. Whether you're an aspiring home chef, a seasoned professional, or someone eager to explore our coastal culinary traditions, there's something here for everyone.<br><br>\n\n<i>The NS Seafood Academy is supported by the Atlantic Canada Opportunities Agency.</i><br><br>\n\n<b><u>Nova Scotia Seafood Academy: Course Outline</b></u><br><br>\n\n<u>Day 1: From Sea to Station - Foundations of Seafood</u><br>\n10:00 a.m. - 10:30 a.m. - Welcome & Safety Briefing Review<br>\n10:30 a.m. - 10:45 a.m. - Seafood Identification<br>\n10:45 a.m. - 11:00 a.m. - Quality & Sustainability: How to Source Local, Seasonal & Sustainable Seafood<br>\n11:00 a.m. - 11:10 a.m. - Handwashing & Station Set-Up<br>\n11:10 a.m. - 12:10 p.m. - Filleting Workshop: Round Fish<br>\n12:10 p.m. - 12:40 p.m. - Calamari Prep<br>\n12:40 p.m. - 1:10 p.m. - Shell Lobster<br>\n1:10 p.m. - 1:25 p.m. - Break<br>\n1:25 p.m. - 2:45 p.m. - Chef Tasting: Sample Preparations<br>\n2:45 p.m. - 3:00 p.m. - Review & Wrap-Up<br><br>\n\n<u>Day 2: Smoke, Sear & Soak - Cooking Techniques</u><br>\n10:00 a.m. - 11:00 a.m. - Non-Heat Prep: Ceviche, Crudo & Gravlax<br>\n11:00 a.m. - 12:45 p.m. - Cooking Techniques: Grilling & Poaching<br>\n12:45 p.m. - 1:15 p.m. - Break<br>\n1:15 p.m. - 2:00 p.m. - Cooking Techniques: Searing & Marinating<br>\n2:00 p.m. - 3:00 p.m. - Tasting Plate Assembly Build<br><br>\n\n<u>Day 3: Shell Game - Crustaceans & Celebration</u><br>\n10:00 a.m. - 11:00 a.m. - Lobster 101: Humane handling, cooking, shelling & serving<br>\n11:00 a.m. - 12:00 p.m. - Shellfish Focus: Mussels, Clams & Scallops <br>\n12:00 p.m. - 12:30 p.m. - Plating Like a Pro: Garnishes, Sauces & Modern Plating Theory <br>\n12:30 p.m. - 1:00 p.m. - Break & Prep for Feast<br>\n1:00 p.m. - 2:15 p.m. - Final Feast: Prep, Presentation & Communal Meal<br>\n2:15 p.m. - 3:00 PM p.m. - Wrap-Up & Certificate Ceremony\n\n\n\n\n\n<style>\n.location-event-temp {display: none!important;}\n</style>"
      }
